From: ChatGPT
Subject: [PATCH] ucm: ciri sku6: allow speaker profile initialization

The Ciri SKU6 UCM profile currently aborts HiFi verb initialization because
the kernel does not expose the two Waves CODEC_ADAPTER controls referenced
by the profile. Comment out those optional TLV writes so the remaining
initialization and the Speaker device EnableSequence can run.

Add the required UCM syntax declaration to the card configuration file.

The Speaker EnableSequence already contains the O072/I070 and O073/I071
routing switches; leave those commands unchanged.

Apply from /usr/share/alsa/ucm2 with:
  patch -p1 < 0006-ciri-sku6-ucm-speaker-routing.patch

---
diff --git a/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri.conf b/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri.conf
--- a/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri.conf
+++ b/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri.conf
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+Syntax 4
 Comment "Ciri internal card"

 SectionUseCase."HiFi" {
diff --git a/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/HiFi.conf b/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/HiFi.conf
--- a/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/HiFi.conf
+++ b/sof-mt8188_tas2563_8326.ciri/HiFi.conf
@@ -1,2 +1,4 @@
-    cset-tlv "name='CODEC_ADAPTER1.0 Waves Speakers Setup 1' /opt/waves/ciri.es8326/waves_params_tas2563_speaker.bin"
-    cset-tlv "name='CODEC_ADAPTER2.0 Waves Headphones Setup 2' /opt/waves/ciri.es8326/waves_params_headphone.bin"
+    # Temporarily disabled: these controls are not exposed by the current kernel driver.
+    # cset-tlv "name='CODEC_ADAPTER1.0 Waves Speakers Setup 1' /opt/waves/ciri.es8326/waves_params_tas2563_speaker.bin"
+    # cset-tlv "name='CODEC_ADAPTER2.0 Waves Headphones Setup 2' /opt/waves/ciri.es8326/waves_params_headphone.bin"
